# YAML frontmatter safety

The consumer site parses every post with `gray-matter` / `js-yaml`. A single bad frontmatter aborts `next build` (`Failed to collect page data for /citadel/...`).

## Required

- Keep the six keys in order: `title`, `description`, `date`, `draft`, `slug`, `tags`.
- Prefer a **double-quoted single-line** `description` (always fine; required when the value has special YAML characters):

```yaml
description: "One to three sentences. Colons like fix: do X are safe here."
```

- Escape internal double quotes as `\"`. Always quote when the value contains `: `, `#`, `{`, `}`, `[`, `]`, `*`, `&`, `!`, `|`, `>`, `%`, `@`, or `` ` ``.

## Forbidden

- Unquoted single-line values that contain `: ` (YAML treats that as a nested mapping and the build dies), e.g. `description: ... show it: reduce ...`.
- Unquoted values that start with `{`, `[`, `*`, `&`, `!`, `|`, `>`, `%`, `@`, or `` ` ``.
- Folded/block scalars (`>-`, `|`) for `description` — keep it one quoted line.

## Before finishing an edit

If the description has a colon (or any character above), double-quote the whole line. When unsure, quote.
